00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.590 align:start position:0%
european union finance and economy  ministers have broken off talks on new  measures to preempt bank crises but plan  to meet again on december 18 to try to  seal a deal by the end of the year  the eco-fin council wants to agree the  terms to establish a single  decision-making authority the so-called  single resolution mechanism and a single  fund to help banks under pressure  we have no formal results in our pocket  or on the table  but we made a huge leap forward  defining the  concrete directions and concrete schemes  that can be further quite  immediately adjusted and discussed with  the  experts of the member states and then  presented  put on the table of the continuation of  the echo finn next week  positions on the proposals a key part of  the eu's ambitious banking union will be  narrowed down by experts ahead of the  december 18 meeting  the aim is to help a struggling credit  institution or investment firm recover  from any shock in an orderly manner  preserving its operations and minimizing  the possibility of taxpayer losses  the measures must be agreed by the  european parliament so eu nations want  to move the package forward before the  assembly's legislative term ends in may  the ministers also sought to reach a  political agreement on rules governing  savings taxation but austria and  luxembourg maintain their reservations  over the proposals which can only be  adopted unanimously  the measures are meant to help fight tax  evasion and tax fraud the council will  report to eu leaders that the proposals  cannot be adopted by the deadline that  they've set
 

